# LF everywhere; Windows contributors get consistent bytes (same rationale as Tinker).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures and any future golden images are binary - never normalized.
#
# The JPEG 2000 pair is named explicitly rather than left to `text=auto`,
# which decides by looking for a NUL in the first 8 KB. Every fixture in the
# tree today happens to have one, but a PGM of an evenly mid-grey image has
# none - and if such a file ever contains the two bytes 0D 0A, committing it
# from Windows would rewrite them and change the picture.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jp2 binary
*.pgm binary

# The XPS corpus (gap 30 milestone 1). These are OPC packages -- ZIPs -- so
# `text=auto` would leave them alone anyway; they are named because the reason
# not to touch them is stronger than "it found a NUL". Every one was written by
# a Microsoft serialiser and none of it is regenerable byte for byte, since both
# serialisers mint a fresh GUID per resource part. A normalised line ending
# inside a stored part would break its CRC-32 and there would be no way back.
*.xps binary
*.oxps binary

# The EPUB corpus (gap 31 milestone 1). OCF containers -- ZIPs again -- named
# for the same reason and one more of its own. `mimetype` is a **stored** entry
# holding exactly twenty ASCII bytes, and OCF 3.3 §4.3.2 requires those twenty
# and no others; a normalised line ending anywhere in a stored entry breaks its
# CRC-32, and there would be no way back, because neither producer is
# reproducible byte for byte -- pandoc and calibre each mint a fresh UUID for
# the package document's `dc:identifier` on every run.
*.epub binary

# Fuzz seeds are bytes chosen for what they make a parser do; a normalized
# line ending is a different input, and several of them have no extension.
fuzz/corpus/** binary

# Adobe's cmap-resources, vendored verbatim (THIRDPARTY.md). `-text` keeps the
# bytes exactly as published, because BSD-3-Clause asks a redistribution to
# retain the notice and normalizing line endings is still a modification.
# `linguist-vendored` collapses eight megabytes of PostScript out of the diff
# a reviewer has to read, and out of the repository's language statistics.
crates/tinker-pdf-font/data/** -text linguist-vendored

# The UCD (gap 31 milestone 7, THIRDPARTY.md). `-text` for cmap-resources'
# reason and one more of its own: the published files are CRLF, the licence
# asks a redistribution to carry the notice, and normalising line endings is
# still a modification. `linguist-vendored` keeps four megabytes of Unicode
# out of the diff a reviewer reads and out of the language statistics.
crates/tinker-pdf-layout/data/** -text linguist-vendored
